! Test 18: H2 dimer BP86-D3(BJ) / 6-31G  [D3 gradient test]
! Two H2 molecules at large separation.  D3(BJ) should give a small
! but nonzero attractive energy and a nonzero force along the
! intermolecular axis.  This test exercises the full C6 interpolation
! + CN-derivative machinery for the simplest nontrivial case.
%method     BP86
%basis      6-31gd
%dispersion D3BJ
%job        opt+freq
%charge     0
%mult       1
%grid       3
%geo
 H   0.000000  0.000000  0.000000
 H   0.740000  0.000000  0.000000
 H   4.000000  0.000000  0.000000
 H   4.740000  0.000000  0.000000

